@startuml
' Primary presentation of the Components-and-Connectors key view.
' Authored in Slice 2. Renders through scripts/render-diagrams.sh.
!include style.puml
title Components-and-Connectors view: primary presentation

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
left to right direction
skinparam nodesep 12
skinparam ranksep 34
skinparam rectangleBorderColor #475569

' ---- store side (one store, drawn in full, x N) -------------------------------
actor "Store\nmanager" as SMGR
node "External\nPOS system" as POS #dae8fc

rectangle "Store  (one of N: 3 now, up to 10)" as STORE {
  component "POS Adapter" as POSAD #dae8fc
  component "Store Agent" as SA #d5e8d4
  database "Store-Local\nInventory" as SLI #e1d5e7
  queue "Outbox" as OB #e1d5e7
}

' ---- distribution center ------------------------------------------------------
rectangle "Distribution Center" as DCB {
  component "Communications\nFront-End\n(pub-sub broker)" as CFE #fff2cc
  database "CFE event\nstore" as CFEDB #e1d5e7
  component "DC Agent" as DCA #fff2cc
  component "Central Master\nInventory" as CMI #fff2cc
  database "Master\ninventory DB" as CMIDB #e1d5e7
  component "Shipping-Order\nFulfillment" as SOG #fff2cc
  component "Supplier Gateway" as SG #dae8fc
  component "Store-Tracking\nClient" as STC #fff2cc
  component "Reporting Client" as RC #fff2cc
}
actor "DC\nmanager" as DMGR
node "External\nsupplier/ERP system" as ERP #dae8fc

' keep the DC manager to the right of the DC box so its query arrows enter from the
' right, clear of the "Distribution Center" boundary title at the top of the box
CMIDB -[hidden]right- DMGR

' ---- connectors ---------------------------------------------------------------
POS --> POSAD : <<request/reply>>\nsales records
POSAD --> SA : <<local call>>\nInventory Events
SMGR --> SA : <<request/reply>>\nlocal inventory queries
SA --> SLI : <<data access>>\napply, read
SA --> OB : <<data access>>\nappend (ordered)
OB --> CFE : <<pub-sub>> publish\nIEP over TLS [secure]
CFE --> OB : <<pub-sub>> acknowledge\nIEP over TLS [secure]
DCA --> CFE : <<pub-sub>> publish
CFE --> CFEDB : <<data access>>\npersist
CFE --> CMI : <<pub-sub>> notify
CFE --> SOG : <<pub-sub>> notify
CFE --> STC : <<pub-sub>> notify
CFE --> RC : <<pub-sub>> notify
CMI --> CMIDB : <<data access>>
SOG --> CMI : <<request/reply>> read
RC --> CMI : <<request/reply>> query
STC --> CMI : <<request/reply>> query
SOG --> SG : <<local call>>\nshipping, purchase orders
SG --> ERP : <<request/reply>>\norders, receipts
DMGR --> RC : <<request/reply>> reports
DMGR --> STC : <<request/reply>> store status

note bottom of CFE
  One n-ary publish-subscribe connector (the Inventory
  Exchange Protocol): the CFE broker joins every publisher
  (store Outboxes, DC Agent) to every subscriber. Drawn once.
end note

legend right
|= Notation |= Meaning |
| green fill | store-side runtime component |
| yellow fill | distribution-center runtime component |
| blue fill | external system or boundary element |
| purple database / queue | durable, ordered persistent store |
| stick figure | human role (store or DC manager), not a component |
| <<pub-sub>> | n-ary publish-subscribe connector (IEP) |
| <<request/reply>> | synchronous request/reply connector |
| <<data access>> | a component reading or writing its own store |
| <<local call>> | in-process hand-off between a component and its boundary element |
| [secure] | a store-to-DC network leg carried over a secure channel |
endlegend
@enduml
